  "title": "All Minimum Bondage Sets of the Truncated-Octahedral Graph, up to Automorphism",
  "batch_label": "49",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the exact 24-vertex, 36-edge labeled graph T in problem.md, the family M(T) of five-edge sets F satisfying gamma(T-F)>gamma(T) has cardinality 276. The full abstract automorphism group Aut(T) has order 48, and M(T) has exactly eight orbits. Under the lexicographic canonical convention of problem.md, their representatives, orbit sizes, setwise stabilizer sizes, and gamma(T-F) values are: [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,4),(1,5)]: (24,2,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,4),(4,9)]: (48,1,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(2,6),(2,7)]: (12,4,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(2,6),(8,14)]: (48,1,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(5,10),(5,11)]: (48,1,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(5,10),(8,14)]: (24,2,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(6,11),(6,12)]: (48,1,9); [(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(6,11),(7,13)]: (24,2,9). These disjoint orbit sizes sum to 276; in particular, every member of M(T) contains the complete three-edge star at some vertex.",
